criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

* Adult male or female (age 18 years or older);
* Having a diagnosis of COPD according to the GOLD (Global Initiative for Lung Disease) 2024 criteria, i.e. a non-reversible bronchial obstruction in spirometry with a post-bronchodilator Tiffeneau coefficient \< 70%;
* Less than or equal to 75 years of age;
* Must benefit from exercise retraining sessions or respiratory rehabilitation as part of the management of COPD;
* Person affiliated to or beneficiary of a social security scheme (excluding State Medical Aid (AME));
* Free, informed and written consent signed by the participant or by a third party (in the event of the participant's physical disability) and the investigator (no later than the day of inclusion and before any review required by the research).

Exclusion Criteria:

* Moderate or severe acute exacerbation of COPD, or acute intercurrent condition (e.g., infection) that has been ongoing or resolved for less than 4 weeks;
* Systemic corticosteroid therapy in progress or stopped for less than 4 weeks;
* Contraindication to respiratory rehabilitation: tight aortic stenosis, unstable heart failure, active thromboembolic disease, ventricular aneurysm, uncontrolled arrhythmias;
* Contraindication to muscle biopsy: acquired or innate haemostasis disorders, anticoagulant treatment or double anti-platelet aggregation; contraindication to lidocaine: known hypersensitivity, patients with recurrent porphyrias;
* Presence of a concomitant muscle pathology, innate (e.g., genetic myopathy) or acquired (e.g., myositis, progressive cancer);
* Pregnant or breastfeeding woman;
* Patient under guardianship or curatorship;
* Refusal to participate in the study.

Exclusion criteria:

\- Hemostasis disorders.
